:"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" holds words,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" the same words scalar by scalar, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" byte strings. Lookup,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a key of "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and at most "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" links, so the trie holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie/Encodable-Implementations":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/Encodable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie\/encodable-implementations","title":"Encodable Implementations","kind":"article"},"doc://Tries/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/SQ"},"doc://Tries/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","title":"Swift.ExpressibleByArrayLiteral"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie/SetAlgebra-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/SetAlgebra-Implementations","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"SetAlgebra Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie\/setalgebra-implementations"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie\/customstringconvertible-implementations","title":"CustomStringConvertible Implementations","kind":"article"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie/elements(withPrefix:)":{"title":"elements(withPrefix:)","abstract":[{"text":"The keys that start with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prefix"},{"text":